{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he sent him from the Valley of Chevron.</b> Scripture mentions the place from which he sent him, to say that there was a great distance between them, and therefore they did evil to him, for they were far from their father, and to tell that Joseph exerted himself for the honor of his father to go after them to a distant place, and did not say, 'How can I go when they hate me?' And to our Sages there is further a midrash in this (Genesis Rabbah 84:13): to fulfill the deep counsel of the Friend [the Patriarch Abraham] who is buried in Chevron."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:58.202730349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}